shell-lsp: fail on a missing reference shell under REQUIRE_REFERENCES

Not for upstream. shell-lsp compares many parsers and formatters with
the tools they mirror, and one variable, REQUIRE_REFERENCES=1, makes
every such comparison fail instead of skip when its reference tool is
missing or of another version; CI sets it where its dev shell provides
each tool at its pinned version. The external shells of
TestParseConfirm and FuzzQuote's bash check go through shell-lsp's
referencetest.Unavailable, which does that, in place of REQUIRE_SHELLS.

diff --git a/syntax/fuzz_test.go b/syntax/fuzz_test.go
index 160fecb..43ee3e5 100644
--- a/syntax/fuzz_test.go
+++ b/syntax/fuzz_test.go
@@ -10,11 +10,13 @@ import (
 	"testing"
 
 	"github.com/go-quicktest/qt"
+
+	"github.com/stubbedev/shell-lsp/internal/referencetest"
 )
 
 func FuzzQuote(f *testing.F) {
 	if _, err := exec.LookPath("bash"); err != nil {
-		f.Skipf("requires bash to verify quoted strings")
+		referencetest.Unavailable(f, "requires bash to verify quoted strings")
 	}
 
 	// Keep in sync with ExampleQuote.
